SUMMARY:System Design — Clarify the handbook brief
DESCRIPTION:Hypothetical brief: a college club publishes a 120-page static 
 handbook. Twenty contributors update it a few times weekly\; it has intern
 al links\, local images and external links. One volunteer maintains publis
 hing. Contributors want useful feedback before publishing\; the editor wan
 ts quick\, dependable publication. No budget for another hosted service or
  dedicated operator. Acceptable delay\, uncertain link results and offline
  operation are undecided.\nIdentify users\, required behavior\, scope and 
 hard constraints. Separate facts\, preferences and assumptions\; ask the q
 uestions that would change a decision. Write checkable acceptance conditio
 ns and defend the dominant requirement. Label how each assumption could be
  tested.\nIf needed\, consult arc42 requirements 1.1–1.3: https://docs.a
 rc42.org/section-1/ and quality scenarios 10.2: https://docs.arc42.org/sec
 tion-10/
END:VEVENT
