SUMMARY:System Design — Independent brief or targeted repair
DESCRIPTION:If your handbook comparison and failure revision are still inco
 mplete\, repair those gaps instead.\nOtherwise\, close teaching sources an
 d try this new brief: a campus club lends 40 pieces of equipment to about 
 150 members. Requests arrive in chat\; one volunteer confirms bookings and
  hands out equipment on weekdays. Members want to see availability and req
 uest slots. No overlapping confirmed bookings for the same item. Administr
 ation should stay low\; uptime\, retention and budget are undecided.\nList
  constraints\, testable assumptions\, unanswered questions and the dominan
 t requirement. Compare two plausible approaches and defend one. Then consi
 der 10× as many members with the same volunteer availability: what change
 s or gets cut first? Stay above database/infrastructure details. Seek crit
 ique only after your attempt.
END:VEVENT
